Investigated Sentry indexing capabilities. Verified that indexed custom fields such as TraceIdentifier are available in Discover and can be added as columns. Tested for the requested X-Test-* headers (X-Test-Run-ID, X-Test-Request-ID, X-Test-Case-ID, etc.) and these fields are not currently available in Discover, indicating they are not being indexed by Sentry. Current assessment is that the application is not sending these values as Sentry tags/fields. Additional development work will likely be required to promote the desired header values to Sentry tags before they can be searched or filtered within Sentry.





Investigated Sentry event indexing using Discover. Verified that fields stored as Tags (e.g. TraceIdentifier) are available in Discover and searchable. Fields stored under Additional Data (e.g. RequestId, ConnectionId, ActionId) are not available as Discover fields and do not appear to be indexed for search. The requested X-Test-* headers (X-Test-Case-ID, X-Test-Name, X-Test-Repo, X-Test-Request-ID, X-Test-Run-ID, X-Test-Spec) are not currently present as indexed Sentry fields/tags. Additional application instrumentation would likely be required to promote these values to Sentry tags before they can be searched or filtered within Discover.
